e},"body":"```cpp\r\nVector3 Quaternion::get_axis() const {\r\n\tif (Math::abs(w) > 1 - CMP_EPSILON) {\r\n\t\treturn Vector3(x, y, z);\r\n\t}\r\n\treal_t r = ((real_t)1) / Math::sqrt(1 - w * w);\r\n\treturn Vector3(x * r, y * r, z * r);\r\n}\r\n```\r\nSince the issue (an error occurs when the rotation is extremely small) stems from the epsilon check in `get_axis()`, so we would need to fix `get_axis()` itself, or, if not, align the epsilon check with `get_axis()` as currently done in this PR.","created_at":"2026-09-28T22:15:56Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T22:22:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123942#discussion_r4127544724","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123942","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/4127544724"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123942#discussion_r4127544724"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123942"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/4127544724/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":90,"original_line":90,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":4127208702,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"}]